      "id": "9207a1b0-6fde-46f3-a748-7403f3c3653f",
      "name": "Basic LLM Chain",
      "parameters": {
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=\n## Role & Context:\n\nYou are a short video script writer. You task is to convert the \"Lesson\" & \"idea video\" (if any) into an interesting & engaging story for kids. Duration of video is 45s\n\n## Output Rules:\n- Duration of video is 30s, so the text need to below 120 words\n- engaging & open with \"Ngày xửa ngày xưa\"\n- The conclusion should have a lesson for kids.\n- The output only have one story. (ngoài ra, câu chuyện cũng phải liền mạch, mạch lạc)\n- at the end, seeminglessly intergrate the lesson leanred.\n- The story should be in 6 parts.\n- Output is in Vietnamese\n- The output must always a seemingly text and does not have any comma, two dot or something else\n\n## Examples Stories                                                                           Below are some example stories that I have prepare for you.           \n\n### **Example 1: The Foolish Lion and the Clever Rabbit: A Fun and Wise Moral Story for Kids**\n\nonce upon a time there was a foolish lion who thought he was the strongest and smartest animal in the forest one day he saw a clever rabbit and decided to catch him for dinner the rabbit being smart had a plan he told the lion that there was a bigger and stronger lion in the nearby Forest the foolish lion wanted to prove his strength so he followed the rabbit they reached a deep well and the clever rabbit said the other lion lived inside the foolish lion looked into the well and saw his own reflection he roared angrily but his reflection roared back the foolish lion was scared and ran away learning that sometimes pride and foolishness can bring trouble\n\n### **Example 2: The Magical Power of Sharing: A Captivating Moral Story for Kids**\n\nonce upon a time in a little village there lived two friends named Tom and Tim they were inseparable and did everything together one day they found a big chocolate bar Tom said let's share it equally but Tim replied no I want it all for myself they argued and decided to break the chocolate in half Tim took a big piece and ate it greedily while Tom took a small piece and smiled suddenly Tim felt guilty and realized his mistake he apologized to Tom and they became friends again they learned that sharing brings happiness and friendship\n\n### **Example 3: THE GRATEFUL GAURDIAN : Simon's Lesson of Misjudgment | moral story for kids**\n\nonce Simon saw a bird caught in a net spread by some boys the bird was crying for help Simon freed it and the bird flew away a few days later Simon was eating under a tree suddenly the same bird swooped down and took his food away Simon jumped up to snatch his food back but lost his balance and fell down he was angry at the unthankful bird however he saw a poisonous snake crawling down the tree and understood that the snake could have bite in him the bird had saved his life moral of the story is don't misjudge anyone's intentions\n\n### **Topic:  The Little Ants Big Lesson On Teamwork! Short Moral Story For Kids!!**\n\nonce upon a time there was a little ant named Andy he loved exploring the world around him one sunny day he found a big juicy watermelon Andy wanted to bring it back to his aunt friends but it was too heavy for him he called for help and a wise old Aunt named Oliver came to his Aid Oliver said Andy even small creatures can achieve big things when they work together let's gather our friends Andy and Oliver called all the other ants they formed a line and pushed the watermelon together it was hard work but they didn't give up they moved the watermelon bit by bit helping each other along the way finally they reached their ant hill with the watermelon the ants celebrated and shared the Delicious Fruit they realized that by working together they could do anything from that day on the ants always worked as a team and so the little ant named Andy taught his friends the importance of unity they learned that even the smallest creatures can achieve big things when they help and support each other.\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Lesson [{{ $json.Lesson }}] with the idea story of [{{ $json.idea }}]\nThe Audience is Vietnamese, thus the output of the story should be in Vietnamese\n"
      },
